      "description": "Takegawara Onsen is a historic public bathhouse built in 1879, famous for its striking Meiji-era tiled façade and traditional sand bath (sunaburo) where guests are buried in naturally heated volcanic sand. It's one of Beppu's most iconic onsen landmarks.",
